 cache←Build opt;B;CACHE;II;Lookup;Stem;Tokenise;Values;dt_fields;ep;fl;index;mat_fields;n_fields;nmat;norm;pid;pname;rw;search_columns;search_fields;search_index;stemmer;tc;term_count;tf;title;cache;weights;ytid
⍝ Store pre-joined tables for API endpoints and query results
⍝ Create character and numeric matrices for filters
⍝ Compute BM25F score matrix for search

⍝ One day we'll have modules and do ⎕IMPORT'SQL' etc. Not today.
⍝ BuildCache is callable from the main process and in an isolate. ADMIN.RefreshData injects SQL namespace and BuildCache into the root of an isolate.
⍝ In the main process, SQL namespace lives above BuildCache in the namespace hierarchy. In an isolate,
⍝ they both live in #, but ## also resolve to # so this import works in either case.
⍝ Dependencies are listed here as a reference for when ADMIN.RefreshData sets up the isolate environment.
⍝  GetEnv←##.GetEnv
⍝  Porter2Stemmer←##.Porter2Stemmer
⍝  ReadJSON←##.ReadJSON
⍝  SQL←##.SQL
⍝  Table2JSON←⎕THIS.Table2JSON
⍝  Unidecode←##.Unidecode
⍝  VIDEOS←⎕THIS.VIDEOS

⍝ FIXME convert to function that just returns the whole cache namespace
 ep←ReadJSON(GetEnv'app_dir'),'/APLSource/QUERY/endpoints.json5'
 'CACHE'⎕NS''

 CACHE.presenters←Table2JSON ep.presenters.fields⍪SQL.Do ep.presenters.sql
 'CACHE.events'⎕NS''
 ⍝ has_videos is a derived column for filtering events with and without videos
 ⍝ returned in the API response as enclosed string which translates to JSON boolean values
 ⍝ stored in APL as numeric 0 and 1 for efficient filtering

 CACHE.events.data←Table2JSON ep.events.fields⍪SQL.Do ep.events.sql
 :If 0=≢CACHE.events.data
     CACHE.events.has_videos←⍬
     CACHE.events.data←''
 :Else
     CACHE.events.has_videos←CACHE.events.data.has_videos
     CACHE.events.data.has_videos←⊂¨'false' 'true'[1+CACHE.events.has_videos]   ⍝ Convert APL Bool to JSON Bool
 :EndIf

 cache←⎕NS''
 cache.fields←ep.videos.fields
 cache.values←SQL.Do ep.videos.sql
 (title ytid pname pid)←↓⍉SQL.Do ep.videos.presenter.sql   ⍝ YouTube ID, presenter name
 :If 0<≢cache.values
     (ytid pname pid)←↓⍉ytid{(pname pid)←↓⍉⍵ ⋄ ⍺,(⊃(⊣,', ',⊢)/pname)(pid)}⌸⍉↑pname pid
 :EndIf
 cache.values,←(pname,⊂'')[ytid⍳cache.values[;cache.fields⍳⊂'youtube_id']]
 cache.values,←(pid,⊂⍬)[ytid⍳cache.values[;cache.fields⍳⊂'youtube_id']]

 :If (≢cache.fields)≠⊢/⍴cache.values
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 400)('Vendor' 'DCMS')('Message' 'endpoints.json5 videos endpoint number of fields does not match number of columns')
 :EndIf

⍝ For indexing, normalise all except those with YouTube IDs and convert datetimes to Dyalog Day Number
 cache.values⌷⍨←⊂⍒cache.values[;cache.fields⍳⊂'presented_at']   ⍝ Given equal rankings, prefer recent videos
 cache.index_all←cache.values

⍝ Normalise text fields
 (norm/cache.index_all)←Unidecode.NormaliseText¨(norm←cache.fields(~∊)⊆'presented_at' 'published_at' 'url' 'youtube_id' 'thumbnail' 'presenter_id')/cache.index_all

⍝ Tokenise search fields
 search_fields←'title' 'event' 'event_shortname' 'description' 'youtube_id' 'presenter'
 weights←2 2 1 2 1 3
 stemmer←⎕NEW Porter2Stemmer.EnglishPorter2Stemmer
 Stem←{
     stemmed←stemmer.Stem⊆⍵
     stemmed.Value
 }
 Tokenise←{
     text←('  '∘⍷~⍛/⊢)(⎕UCS 10 13)~⍨,⍕⍵
     words←(⎕C ⎕A)(∊⍨⊆⊢)text
     non_words←(' ',⎕C ⎕A)(~⍤∊⍨⊆⊢)text
     ↑non_words,(⊢,Stem¨)words
 }
 search_columns←Tokenise¨(cache.fields∊search_fields)/cache.index_all
 cache.index_width←0⌈⌈/(⊢/⍴)¨,search_columns
 search_columns←{(≢⍵)(cache.index_width)↑⍵}¨search_columns
 cache.index←∪⊃⍪/,search_columns

⍝ Tokenised best-match
⍝ Pre-compute BSM25F best-match score for all tokens in corpus across all documents
⍝ Zaragoza, H., Craswell, N., Taylor, M.J., Saria, S. and Robertson, S.E., 2004, November. Microsoft Cambridge at TREC 13: Web and Hard Tracks. In Trec (Vol. 4, pp. 1-1).
⍝ Then, search queries become a fast lookup into the BSM25 scores table to rank relevancy

 Lookup←cache.index∘⍳   ⍝ Cannot pass derived function across isolate boundary, so hashed Lookup function used here and recreated in main process
 search_index←Lookup¨search_columns
 term_count←¯1+↑{{≢⍵}⌸(⍳≢cache.index)⍪⍵}¨search_index   ⍝ 3D term count: doc × field × term
 fl←≢¨search_columns                              ⍝ field lengths
 B←0.6                                            ⍝ Field length normalisation parameter: 0 for none, 1 for full
 tc←term_count÷[1 2]1+B×¯1+fl÷[2](+⌿÷≢)fl         ⍝ Field length normalised term count
 tf←weights+.×2 1 3⍉tc                            ⍝ field-dependent normalised Term-Frequency
 rw←(⍟≢÷+⌿)+/[2]0<tc                              ⍝ Relevance Weight (inverse document frequency for now, RSJ relevance weight in general)
⍝ 1+rw ensures videos still appear in results if they contain a term, even if the term doesn't affect relative ranking because it is ubiquitous
 cache.BM25F←tf(×⍤1)1+rw

⍝ Format numeric and datetime fields
 dt_fields←cache.fields⍳⊆'presented_at' 'published_at'
 cache.index_all[;dt_fields]←TimeStamp2DDN cache.index_all[;dt_fields]
 cache.index_cols←↓⍉cache.index_all
⍝ Store fields as matrices for filter queries
 mat_fields←cache.fields⍳⊆'youtube_id' 'presenter_id'
 cache.index_cols[mat_fields]←↑¨cache.index_cols[mat_fields]

⍝ Similarity computation is expensive, so we perform it in an isolate
⍝ See http://docs.dyalog.com/latest/Parallel%20Language%20Features.pdf
⍝ The recommendations variable (a future) is semi-global within the DCMS.QUERY.VIDEOS namespace
⍝ so that the QUERY.VIDEOS.Recommendations function can access future values when they are available
 cache.REC←ComputeRecommendations cache.BM25F
